1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,516
This is the last lecture of the class,

2
00:00:02,966 --> 00:00:05,453
and it teaches no new word.

3
00:00:07,253 --> 00:00:10,244
You're going to write your own long away mission.

4
00:00:11,144 --> 00:00:14,168
Three areas, a quest tree, and two endings.

5
00:00:14,618 --> 00:00:17,919
Three jobs, each with something only that person can do.

6
00:00:19,719 --> 00:00:22,309
I'll show you mine, start to finish.

7
00:00:22,759 --> 00:00:25,420
It's small on purpose, so you can read all of it.

8
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:29,890
Then you write yours.

9
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:34,914
Start on paper, with the same three sentences as the sixth lecture.

10
00:00:35,814 --> 00:00:38,309
The question, and the answer found in pieces.

11
00:00:38,759 --> 00:00:40,189
And the choice at the end.

12
00:00:41,989 --> 00:00:43,398
Mine is a mine.

13
00:00:43,848 --> 00:00:45,853
Four diggers behind a rock fall.

14
00:00:46,753 --> 00:00:48,379
Dig them out and keep the mine,

15
00:00:48,829 --> 00:00:50,785
or blast them out and lose it.

16
00:00:52,585 --> 00:00:54,343
Then the beat sheet from last time.

17
00:00:55,243 --> 00:00:58,225
A landing, three tracks, a join,

18
00:00:58,675 --> 00:01:00,571
a last area, and an ending.

19
00:01:01,021 --> 00:01:02,949
With minutes beside each one.

20
00:01:04,149 --> 00:01:06,748
Here's my middle area on the engineer's console,

21
00:01:07,198 --> 00:01:09,886
the chief at the gate, and the ore hauler in the yard.

22
00:01:10,786 --> 00:01:13,066
The lift house itself is still in fog.

23
00:01:14,866 --> 00:01:18,467
In the files, three areas, and one decision each.

24
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:21,317
The camp is where they land.

25
00:01:22,217 --> 00:01:24,230
The lift house has to be found once.

26
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,489
After that the ship can put you there.

27
00:01:27,389 --> 00:01:29,876
And the gallery can't be beamed into at all.

28
00:01:30,326 --> 00:01:32,018
That's what makes the lift matter.

29
00:01:33,818 --> 00:01:36,146
Look at the map with last week's eyes.

30
00:01:37,046 --> 00:01:39,346
Every mark is the name of a place.

31
00:01:39,796 --> 00:01:41,726
Nothing hidden stands on a mark.

32
00:01:42,626 --> 00:01:45,725
And the titles read well after the words go to.

33
00:01:46,925 --> 00:01:49,452
Draw three columns before you write a single prop.

34
00:01:49,902 --> 00:01:52,114
Who's doing what, in each beat?

35
00:01:53,914 --> 00:01:55,342
Then the hard part of the brief.

36
00:01:55,792 --> 00:01:58,886
Each job gets one thing nobody else can do.

37
00:01:59,786 --> 00:02:01,941
Here's one, on the doctor's handheld.

38
00:02:02,391 --> 00:02:05,624
Only someone that good is offered Set his leg.

39
00:02:07,424 --> 00:02:08,824
There are two ways to write that.

40
00:02:09,274 --> 00:02:12,773
A skill on an answer, or needs on a prop.

41
00:02:13,673 --> 00:02:15,136
It can't be a job,

42
00:02:15,586 --> 00:02:18,853
because a job is covered by whoever's in the scene.

43
00:02:20,653 --> 00:02:22,842
And here's the rule that keeps it fair.

44
00:02:23,742 --> 00:02:25,838
A thing only one person can do

45
00:02:26,288 --> 00:02:27,975
must never be the only road.

46
00:02:29,775 --> 00:02:32,261
So the cheap ending is open to anybody.

47
00:02:33,161 --> 00:02:35,083
The good ending has two doors,

48
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:37,315
and each one needs somebody.

49
00:02:38,515 --> 00:02:39,505
Now the quest tree.

50
00:02:39,955 --> 00:02:43,798
Remember what the bridge gets: the shared quests, and nothing else.

51
00:02:44,698 --> 00:02:47,832
So this tree is the story the bridge follows.

52
00:02:49,632 --> 00:02:51,375
One arc, with the clock on it.

53
00:02:52,275 --> 00:02:55,405
The arc waits, and the first answer on the ground starts it.

54
00:02:55,855 --> 00:02:58,416
So nobody loses time choosing a console.

55
00:03:00,216 --> 00:03:01,965
Each step is news for the ship.

56
00:03:02,865 --> 00:03:05,354
And the two endings are the last two steps,

57
00:03:05,804 --> 00:03:08,057
each with its own winning sentence.

58
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:11,373
I got this wrong the first time.

59
00:03:11,823 --> 00:03:14,604
I had the endings outside the arc.

60
00:03:15,504 --> 00:03:18,004
The arc finished early, and the clock stopped with it.

61
00:03:18,454 --> 00:03:21,458
Keep the endings inside, and waiting.

62
00:03:23,258 --> 00:03:26,470
And the arc's description is the bridge's briefing.

63
00:03:27,370 --> 00:03:29,715
Nobody aboard hears Ada Corvin,

64
00:03:30,165 --> 00:03:32,265
so the arc says what she said.

65
00:03:33,165 --> 00:03:35,638
Who's where, in a table,

66
00:03:36,088 --> 00:03:38,978
and the air she counted, on an hourglass line.

67
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,480
Both endings live in one room.

68
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:46,034
Here's the rock fall on the engineer's handheld,

69
00:03:46,484 --> 00:03:48,747
once the party knows all four things.

70
00:03:50,547 --> 00:03:53,295
In the file, a choice has one condition,

71
00:03:53,745 --> 00:03:56,491
so a thing that needs two takes two rooms.

72
00:03:56,941 --> 00:03:59,325
Facts in the first, and the jacks in the second.

73
00:04:01,125 --> 00:04:02,559
Now something to plan for.

74
00:04:03,459 --> 00:04:05,577
A shot never removes a prop.

75
00:04:06,477 --> 00:04:08,665
Shoot the lift gate, and it stays shut,

76
00:04:09,115 --> 00:04:11,615
because only the lift's own signal opens it.

77
00:04:12,515 --> 00:04:14,729
And nothing on the handheld mentions the shot.

78
00:04:15,179 --> 00:04:17,623
Look still shows the last thing picked up.

79
00:04:18,523 --> 00:04:21,323
Shoot the rock fall, and both endings are still there.

80
00:04:23,124 --> 00:04:25,197
A door opens to a shot

81
00:04:25,647 --> 00:04:28,595
only when its Opens with line says cut.

82
00:04:29,495 --> 00:04:31,745
So ask one question of your own mission.

83
00:04:32,195 --> 00:04:35,106
Which doors should the crew be able to force?

84
00:04:36,306 --> 00:04:37,710
Lint reads your spelling.

85
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,736
It doesn't walk your map.

86
00:04:40,636 --> 00:04:44,092
So here are the checks of the whole class, on one sheet.

87
00:04:44,542 --> 00:04:46,112
Twelve of them, in order.

88
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:49,506
Ways in and ways out.

89
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:51,748
Keys and names that join.

90
00:04:52,198 --> 00:04:53,662
Signals with two ends.

91
00:04:54,562 --> 00:04:57,189
Then the worst party, and the three columns.

92
00:04:57,639 --> 00:05:01,037
The screen, a full shot, and the clock.

93
00:05:02,837 --> 00:05:04,463
Then walk it, every road.

94
00:05:05,363 --> 00:05:08,756
On the way, somebody has to stop the hauler for its coupling.

95
00:05:09,206 --> 00:05:14,424
Stand on the works gate, outside its notice, and fire one full shot.

96
00:05:15,324 --> 00:05:17,780
Click the cell it has just stepped onto,

97
00:05:18,230 --> 00:05:20,375
as it walks up the west side of its square.

98
00:05:21,275 --> 00:05:23,041
Shots miss a lot,

99
00:05:23,491 --> 00:05:26,306
and no app tells you a shot hit or missed.

100
00:05:28,106 --> 00:05:30,331
A doctor and an engineer dig them out.

101
00:05:31,231 --> 00:05:35,277
One person alone, using no skill at all, blasts them out.

102
00:05:37,077 --> 00:05:40,039
The times on the page are floors from a script.

103
00:05:40,489 --> 00:05:43,668
Walk yours with people, and write down what you get.

104
00:05:44,868 --> 00:05:46,968
Here's the rubric, in ten lines,

105
00:05:47,418 --> 00:05:49,333
and each one has a way to know.

106
00:05:51,133 --> 00:05:55,030
Three areas. A quest tree. Two endings and a way to lose.

107
00:05:55,930 --> 00:05:58,118
Three jobs nobody can replace.

108
00:05:58,568 --> 00:06:00,364
A clock that starts on the ground.

109
00:06:01,264 --> 00:06:03,595
An ending for the smallest party.

110
00:06:04,045 --> 00:06:06,053
And work for three at once.

111
00:06:07,853 --> 00:06:09,918
You're done when every line is ticked,

112
00:06:10,368 --> 00:06:12,128
and when somebody who didn't write it

113
00:06:12,578 --> 00:06:15,602
has played it to an ending without asking you anything.

114
00:06:17,402 --> 00:06:19,218
That's the end of Boarding Parties.

115
00:06:19,668 --> 00:06:21,056
Now go and write yours.
